xnu 0435: take over the fault route for PCIe SID 0x1c00

The bootloader leaves SMR slot 7 valid for SID 0x1c00 with S2CR type 2
(translation fault in SMMU-v2), so W6's second-SID attach refused the route and
the load failed cleanly instead of resetting. Type 0 is another translating
context and stays a conflict; type 1/2 is bypass/fault and belongs to the WLAN
function. Repoint those to the same bank, save the old SMR/S2CR, and restore
them in teardown.

Measured before this change: sid2 0x1c00 conflicts slot 7 smr=0x80001c00
s2cr=0x20000, then W6 SMMU map failed; the 4 KiB BHI load returned failed
instead of resetting the SoC.

